---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DeviceScreen from '../../components/DeviceScreen.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/url';
import presetScreen from '../../assets/device/01-preset.png';
import editScreen from '../../assets/device/02-edit.png';
import modulesScreen from '../../assets/device/30-modules.png';
import ratScreen from '../../assets/device/20-param-rat.png';
import eqScreen from '../../assets/device/17-param-eq.png';
import tunerScreen from '../../assets/device/40-tuner.png';

const docSizes = '(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 52rem';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="UI & Controls"
  description="Use the Ardor touchscreen, four footswitches, and encoder to choose sounds, edit a chain, and tune."
  lede="The Ardor screen is made for playing. Choose a preset with your foot, change a sound on the touch display, and follow the chain from left to right."
>
  <h2>Preset screen</h2>
  <DeviceScreen src={presetScreen} alt="Preset screen: bank 01 with four preset tiles. Clean Lead is live in red." caption="The home screen: four slots in the active bank. The live preset is red." glow={{ x: 26, y: 26, strength: 'soft' }} sizes={docSizes} />
  <p>
    The header shows the bank number and name. Each tile shows its footswitch, the preset name,
    and its chain in family colors. The live preset fills with red. The controls at the bottom are:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Edit</strong> opens the chain editor for the live preset.</li>
    <li><strong>Tuner</strong> opens the chromatic tuner.</li>
    <li><strong>Looper</strong> opens the four-track looper.</li>
    <li><strong>Bank −</strong> and <strong>Bank +</strong> move to the previous or next bank.</li>
    <li><strong>Setup</strong> opens the settings: appearance, Wi-Fi, audio, controls, and updates.</li>
    <li><strong>Master</strong> shows the output volume. Turn the encoder to change it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Edit a sound</h2>
  <DeviceScreen src={editScreen} alt="Chain editor: compressor, Clean Twin amp, open back 2x12 cabinet, chorus switched off, and tape delay, from left to right." caption="The chain runs from the input at the left to the output at the right." sizes={docSizes} />
  <p>
    The editor shows the signal from left to right. Your guitar enters at the left. Each
    effect appears in the order that it runs. The output is at the right. Scroll the canvas
    sideways when a chain is longer than the screen.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Tap <strong>+</strong> between two blocks to add an effect.</li>
    <li>Tap a block to open its controls.</li>
    <li>Drag a block to change its place in the chain.</li>
    <li>Tap <strong>Modules</strong>, then use the family buttons to find amps, cabinets, drives, delays, reverbs, and other blocks.</li>
    <li>Tap <strong>Save</strong> when you want to keep the change. Tap <strong>Undo</strong> to go back one step.</li>
  </ol>
  <DeviceScreen src={modulesScreen} alt="Modules drawer: family filter buttons and a list of amp captures, each with a plus button." caption="The Modules drawer. Tap + to insert a block, or hold a block to drag it." sizes={docSizes} />
  <p>
    Choose <strong>Split Left / Right</strong> in the Modules drawer when you want two lanes. See{' '}
    <a href={url('/docs/dual-rig')}>Dual Rig &amp; Dual Amp</a> for the two-lane layout.
  </p>

  <h2>Change effect controls</h2>
  <DeviceScreen src={ratScreen} alt="RAT Distortion controls: Distortion, Filter, and Volume sliders. Distortion has a red outline and an ENC mark." caption="The encoder edits the control with the red outline and the ENC mark." glow={{ x: 18, y: 48, strength: 'soft' }} sizes={docSizes} />
  <p>
    Each block shows its controls as large sliders with the name and the value. Drag a slider, or
    turn the encoder to change the control with the <strong>ENC</strong> mark. Use <strong>−</strong>
    and <strong>+</strong> for fine steps. Tap <strong>Block On</strong> to bypass the block and hear
    the sound without it.
  </p>
  <DeviceScreen src={eqScreen} alt="Five-band EQ page: a response graph with high-pass, five bands, and low-pass, and sliders for frequency, Q, and gain." caption="The five-band EQ has its own page with a live response graph." sizes={docSizes} />

  <h2>Tuner</h2>
  <DeviceScreen src={tunerScreen} alt="Tuner screen: E2 at 82.4 Hz, minus 2 cents, in tune, with the output muted." caption="The tuner mutes the output while you tune." glow={{ x: 50, y: 30, strength: 'soft' }} sizes={docSizes} />
  <p>
    The tuner shows the note, frequency, and whether the note is flat or sharp. It mutes the
    output while it is open. Tap the on-screen exit button, or press any footswitch, to
    leave the tuner.
  </p>

  <h2>Footswitches and encoder</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td class="mono">Footswitch 1 to 4</td><td>Choose preset slot 1 to 4 in the active bank.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="mono">Encoder</td><td>Change the master output volume.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="mono">Hold FS1 + FS2</td><td>Hold for one second to mute and open the tuner.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Any footswitch</td><td>Leave the tuner without changing the preset.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      If you change the preset or bank with unsaved edits, Ardor asks whether to{' '}
      <strong>Save</strong>,
      <strong>Discard</strong>, or <strong>Cancel</strong>. Your draft
      does not disappear without a choice.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    You can also control presets and effect parameters with MIDI or an expression pedal. See
    the <a href={url('/docs/hardware')}>Hardware guide</a> for the optional connections.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
